From 13f8a627ee82419561c087becc7f9f6badbdd9f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:30:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Compact idle chats before their prompt cache expires
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Claude chat left idle past its prompt cache's lifetime pays to send its
whole context again with the next message. Now, when a Claude turn ends,
the engine arms a timer 2 min before the cache expires (the last
request's start plus its TTL, an hour; a read carries the TTL before it
forward), in memory only. When it fires, a chat still idle and eligible
gets `/compact` as a run of the engine's own resuming its session: the
setting on and the chat's own choice not off, Claude Code, at least 200k
tokens, not a subagent or side chat, not archived, no question pending, no
background work, nothing queued, no turn running. A compaction arms
nothing (once an idle spell); a message sent while one runs waits in the
queue for it rather than steering it.

The transcript shows one divider for a compaction, the engine's or a
typed `/compact` alike: "Compacting 240k tokens…", then "Compacted 240k →
18k tokens", opening the summary (from Claude's `compact_boundary` and the
summary message after it). A bare `/compact` prompt shows as its divider;
the engine's own writes no user message. The composer's alerts say "Next
message resends 240k tokens" on a top-level Claude chat of 200k+ tokens
whose cache expired, with Compact chat (sends `/compact`) and ×, which puts
it away until the cache expires again; hidden while a command is typed.
Settings → General has "Compact idle chats" (default on, the engine's
harness-prefs.json); a Claude chat's menu has "Compact when idle", its own
choice over the setting (the chat row's `compactIdle`).

Claude Code's `conversation_reset` (`/clear`) now empties the context the
chat shows, so the alert's count starts again.

ZERON_IDLE_COMPACT_AFTER_MS (fire that long after the last request) and
ZERON_IDLE_COMPACT_MIN_TOKENS shorten it for a live check
(crates/engine/tests/idle_compact_live.rs, ignored: one real turn, then
the engine's own compaction, warm or after the agent's idle stop).
